ai-trading-analyst
==================

This plugin vendors skills from an upstream open-source project:

    Repository: https://github.com/zubair-trabzada/ai-trading-claude
    License:    MIT (see ./LICENSE)
    Snapshot:   c6d7252211a72405cefaff3e62d27a032c58348c (main branch)
    Vendored:   2026-05-11

Vendored skills (under skills/):
    trade-analyze, trade-thesis, trade-risk,
    trade-fundamental, trade-technical, trade-sentiment,
    trade-earnings, trade-options

Vendored helper scripts (under scripts/):
    generate_trade_html.py
        Used by trade-analyze to render the JSON payload it writes to
        /tmp/trade_report_data.json into a self-contained HTML file.
        Stdlib-only, no external dependencies. The web app's wrapper
        prompt points trade-analyze at this vendored copy instead of
        the upstream ~/.claude/skills/trade/scripts/ location.

Not vendored (out of scope for the Analysis tab UI):
    trade, trade-quick, trade-compare, trade-screen, trade-watchlist,
    trade-portfolio, trade-sector, trade-report-pdf, generate_trade_pdf.py
        trade-quick is intentionally excluded: its SKILL.md is terminal-only
        ("Do NOT write any files") and cannot be reliably coerced into a
        single-HTML-file pipeline.

Local modifications: none. SKILL.md and script files are byte-for-byte
copies from the upstream snapshot. The wrapper prompt issued by
`app/trade_plan_runner.py` overrides per-skill output instructions where
needed (e.g. markdown-only skills are told to render HTML inline instead).
If a skill diverges from this behaviour, raise an issue against this repo
rather than modifying the vendored files in place.
